Physical Exam: Abdominal exam reveals gross distension and diffuse, mild tenderness to deep palpation across all four quadrants without guarding, rigidity, or rebound tenderness. Bowel sounds are present but hyperactive. Oral examination shows a distinct, thick white plaque on the dorsal tongue consistent with candidal overgrowth, and notable halitosis. Musculoskeletal exam yields diffuse, non-focal migrating joint aching without objective swelling or warmth. Neurological exam reveals intact cranial nerves but obvious cognitive sluggishness. The presentation is highly consistent with chronic abdominal bloating, altered bowel habits, brain fog, and migrating joint aching. Confirmation requires comprehensive DNA-based stool analysis indicating pathogenic overgrowth.
